  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote the whole game in `src/main.ts`. It typechecks, but I couldn't run it or `vite build` in this sandbox, so how it looks and plays is untested.\n\n- **Scene:** The `neon-arcade` look with bloom, a perspective camera, and a 3×3 grid of stone pedestals, each with a dark hole. Lanterns (amber body with brass cap and base) rise out of the holes. Bombs are dark spheres with a fuse and a pulsing red spark.\n- **Rules:**\n  - A seeded RNG drives spawns, taken from `?seed=` or a default. Each restart re-seeds, so a seed repeats the spawn order.\n  - Lantern visible time and the spawn gap both shrink as the score rises.\n  - Popping a lantern gives +10 and a gold burst. Clicking an empty cell, or a lantern that is already sinking, costs 5 (floored at 0) and shows a red flash and red sparks.\n  - Clicking a bomb ends the run as `lost`.\n  - The 45 s timer ends the round as `won` at 150 points or more, otherwise `lost`.\n  - A cyan highlight follows the pointer.\n- **Picking:** Clicks are resolved with ray math against the camera I set, assuming the engine uses a vertical field of view in degrees (the engine source suggests it does). If that assumption is wrong, clicks would land off-target.\n- **HUD and controls:**\n  - A DOM HUD sits below the canvas with score, time and status. An overlay over the canvas shows the Start button, and later Restart and the result.\n  - Enter starts from `ready`. R restarts from any state.\n- **State and ready flag:**\n  - `window.__TASK_STATE__` is updated every frame. `activeCells` lists cells that are rising or fully up.\n  - `window.__TASK_READY__` is set about two animation frames after `app.ready()` resolves.\n\n",
